 *   **Cell Boundaries:** Numerical issues arise when the ray origin is near the edge of a cell. The method mitigates this by setting the local cell position to the midpoint of the ray's overlap with the cell [S4, unofficial].
 *   **Gradient Artifacts:** When computing normals, clamping in the gradient computation can produce artifacts at cell boundaries. Reducing `delta_step` reduces these artifacts but may make the surface appear bumpier due to less smooth normals [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Sign Changes:** The algorithm relies on detecting sign changes. If the isovalue is exactly equal to a corner value or a critical point, special handling (e.g., epsilon comparison) is required [G].
